   "isContainedBy": "https://github.com/prism-science/sampleworks",
   "title": "sampleworks README, contributions wanted"
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:q3",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - How can structure predictors, guidance methods and loss functions be compared on equal terms?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Each published guidance method is built for one predictor and tested on its own small set of examples, so results cannot be compared."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Introduction, paragraphs 5-6",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2406.04239",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2506.04490",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2602.05285",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-026-03047-4",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2502.09372",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2602.24007",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2605.15564"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:q1",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Can structure predictors recover experimentally supported alternative conformations when guided by density maps?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Tested on 791 altloc segments from 40 high-resolution X-ray PDB entries, guided by simulated, noise-free maps."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Purpose; Results: 'A dataset of 40 PDB entries with 791 alternative location segments'",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sbi.2014.07.005",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2052252524005098"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:q4",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - What guidance strength improves fit to density without breaking model geometry?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Stronger guidance pulls harder toward the map but can push atoms into chemically impossible positions."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Results: 'Guidance with density maps improves conformational sampling...', Figure 3B",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2602.05285",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2502.09372"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:q2",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Have structure predictors learned physical energy landscapes, or do they memorize training conformations?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Altlocs are removed from all current training sets. They are physically plausible but absent from training data, which makes them a test of memorization."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Introduction, final paragraphs; Results: dataset section",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07487-w",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-51801-z",
    "https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.02.05.703733"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c1",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - A framework with four swappable parts (ModelWrappers, LossFunctions, Samplers, Scalers) lets predictors and guidance methods be compared on the same data",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Adding a predictor only requires a featurize method and a step method. Any differentiable loss can be plugged in."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Results: 'sampleworks is a plug-and-play platform...', Figure 1",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.01.08.631967",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.06.14.659707",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2406.04239",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2502.09372",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.08.14.670328",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2209.14687",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2501.06848",
    "https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.11.19.624167"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c2",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Without guidance, predicted ensembles collapse toward one conformation",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Across 8 random seeds per target, predictors rarely produce both deposited altlocs."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Purpose; Results: 'Without guidance, structure predictors are strongly biased...', Figure 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.82153/jkxj-tw08#quote-c2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c3",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Density guidance improves fit to the map for every predictor tested",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Fit is measured by real-space correlation coefficient (RSCC) between the predicted-ensemble map and the target map."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Results: density guidance section, Figure 3; Discussion, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2506.04490",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-026-03047-4",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2502.09372",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2605.15564"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c4",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Guidance does not reliably recover both deposited conformations",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Better fit can come from fitting one altloc more closely, or from new conformations that are not the deposited ones."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Results: density guidance section, Figure 3D-E"
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c6",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Predictors respond differently to the same guidance on the same protein",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Differences often mirror each predictor's baseline behavior and training data."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Results: 'Inconsistent gains across structure predictors...', Figure 5",
   "references": [
