  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c7",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Too much guidance degrades geometry and, past a point, also worsens fit",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The authors suggest very large steps along the density gradient destabilize the sampling trajectory."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Results: density guidance section, Figure 3B; Supplementary Figure 4",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2602.05285",
    "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2502.09372"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c5",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Guided ensembles still follow the conformation mix found in the training set",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Guidance reduces this bias but does not remove it. The authors describe this as memorization."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Results: 'Guided structure predictors reflect memorization of the training set', Figure 4",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-51801-z",
    "https://doi.org/10.7554/elife.36307"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "sw:c8",
   "@type": [
    "sw:schema-Claim",
    "mira:Claim"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "CLM - Predictors have learned enough physics to sample near-isoenergetic alternative states",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "The hypothesis the benchmark was designed to test. Equal-occupancy altlocs are close in energy, so a physics-aware model should sample both, especially when guided. The evidence opposes it."
   },
   "creator": "sw:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Chrispens et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/jkxj-tw08. Introduction, final two paragraphs; Discussion, paragraph 2",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-51801-z",
    "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.adv9817"
   ]
  },
